<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Kano is the largest manufacturing and commercial centre in northern Nigeria, and almost every plant in it treats grid supply as a supplement rather than a baseline. Tanneries in Challawa and Sharada, flour and food processing lines in Bompai, textile and plastics plants around Dakata, and the agro-processing yards handling groundnut, sesame and hides and skins all run their production hours on captive generation. That makes the generator hall a process asset rather than a standby asset, and it changes how the equipment has to be maintained.</p><p>We deliver <a href="/generator-maintenance-nigeria/">generator maintenance</a>, <a href="/steam-turbine-overhaul-nigeria/">steam and gas turbine overhaul</a> and <a href="/rotating-equipment-services-nigeria/">rotating equipment services</a> to industrial sites across Kano State from our Lagos base. Kano carries a heavy installed base of medium and high capacity sets with very few providers able to strip, measure and rebuild one properly, so a lot of plant here is being kept alive by parts changing rather than engineering. Every scope we quote begins with measurement: load profile, running hours, oil and coolant condition, vibration signature and thermal survey, then a written proposal with defined work content and a fixed outage window.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Kano</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Kano Plants</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Diesel generator overhaul and top end repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Top end and full overhauls on sets from 250 kVA to 2.5 MVA that carry the long daily runs normal for Kano industry. We work to running hours and oil analysis results rather than the calendar, because a set on 16 hours a day reaches a 12,000 hour overhaul point in well under three years.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Planned maintenance and condition monitoring contracts</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Scheduled visits covering oil and coolant sampling, vibration readings, load bank testing and thermographic checks on alternators, breakers and busbars. Dust loading in Kano means filter, breather and radiator intervals here are shorter than the OEM figures written for temperate installations.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Steam and gas turbine overhaul</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Combustion and hot gas path inspections, rotor and blade assessment, bearing and seal work and full major overhauls, including the back pressure steam turbines found on boiler equipped textile, tannery and food processing plants. We also assess dual fuel and CNG readiness as gas supply moves north.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Rotating equipment, pumps and drive trains</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Laser shaft alignment, dynamic balancing, bearing and seal replacement and gearbox repair on process pumps, boiler feed sets, air compressors, blowers, dryers and tannery drum drives. Misalignment, bearing failure and dust ingress are the failure modes we are called to most often on Kano production lines.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
